WEBVTT

00:01:35.050 --> 00:01:40.470
<b>12. The Chosen Maiden</b>

00:01:36.170 --> 00:01:38.050
I've been waiting for you,

00:01:38.860 --> 00:01:40.800
...Fena Houtman.

00:01:41.420 --> 00:01:43.200
Who is this?

00:01:43.680 --> 00:01:45.380
Cody...

00:01:45.920 --> 00:01:47.180
What do you mean?

00:01:47.700 --> 00:01:48.690
In short,

00:01:49.360 --> 00:01:52.690
...all of the elements that lead
to you standing in this place...

00:01:53.330 --> 00:01:56.320
...were set into motion by us.

00:01:57.080 --> 00:01:59.570
I am a part of Eden,

00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:02.330
...and Eden is a part of me.

00:02:03.580 --> 00:02:06.580
It is we who govern the bloodline
of the maidens, and their lives,

00:02:07.080 --> 00:02:09.080
...and guide them to this place.

00:02:11.080 --> 00:02:12.970
Are you ready?

00:02:24.640 --> 00:02:26.200
What is this place?

00:02:28.470 --> 00:02:29.870
Yukimaru?

00:02:31.140 --> 00:02:33.140
- Yukimaru?!
- This is the entrance.

00:02:36.340 --> 00:02:38.110
Cody...

00:02:39.780 --> 00:02:41.340
What is this place?!
Where's Yukimaru?!

00:02:41.440 --> 00:02:45.080
He is safe,
Fena La Pucelle Frederick.

00:02:45.530 --> 00:02:48.060
Princess, true daughter
of the king of England.

00:02:50.580 --> 00:02:54.830
As well as the daughter of
Helena La Pucelle des Armoises.

00:02:56.670 --> 00:03:00.020
You guided me here?

00:03:00.360 --> 00:03:02.340
Not just me.

00:03:03.010 --> 00:03:07.080
The breadcrumbs and visions
you experienced on your journey

00:03:07.180 --> 00:03:09.430
belonged to a previous maiden,
Johanne La Pucelle.

00:03:12.200 --> 00:03:14.280
Your distant ancestor.

00:03:15.110 --> 00:03:19.060
Memories from a past maiden
that she entrusted to you.

00:03:19.490 --> 00:03:22.570
As well as the preordained fate
possessed by you yourself.

00:03:24.070 --> 00:03:28.450
Every moment conspired to weave together
the story that is you.

00:03:29.830 --> 00:03:31.080
It was all...

00:03:31.880 --> 00:03:36.660
...a test to determine if you have
what it takes to be a maiden.

00:03:37.080 --> 00:03:39.340
And you demonstrated
that you do.

00:03:40.170 --> 00:03:46.130
You chose from the options presented to you
and found your way to this place.

00:03:50.220 --> 00:03:51.930
Chose...?

00:03:53.190 --> 00:03:56.490
I thought I was making choices,
but I was being <i>made</i> to choose.

00:03:57.770 --> 00:04:00.490
By that mysterious part
of me again...

00:04:01.940 --> 00:04:03.670
What do you want to
make me do now?

00:04:03.770 --> 00:04:05.380
You want something, don't you?!

00:04:05.480 --> 00:04:06.700
Tell me!

00:04:09.560 --> 00:04:11.520
We searched.

00:04:11.580 --> 00:04:16.080
For a being who would manage the swollen
number of souls in our stead.

00:04:17.910 --> 00:04:25.470
And so we choose. We would have that being
test humanity and ascertain their maturity.

00:04:26.590 --> 00:04:30.870
That was how the Maiden
of Choosing came to be.

00:04:32.610 --> 00:04:37.980
Through countless cycles of death and rebirth,
they have continued to make that choice.

00:04:40.420 --> 00:04:41.980
What choice?

00:04:43.060 --> 00:04:47.360
Destruction and creation.
Or continuation.

00:04:48.250 --> 00:04:49.490
In short,

00:04:50.110 --> 00:04:52.640
...to destroy the world,

00:04:53.060 --> 00:04:54.860
...or leave it be.

00:05:02.330 --> 00:05:04.130
To choose.

00:05:05.000 --> 00:05:09.760
That is your role as one born
to be the Maiden of Choosing.

00:05:11.600 --> 00:05:15.030
What are you saying?
Destroy the world? Leave it be?

00:05:15.130 --> 00:05:17.540
How can I possibly make a choice
like that at the drop of a hat?!

00:05:17.640 --> 00:05:22.380
Will civilization's end come now,
or in the distant future?

00:05:23.030 --> 00:05:26.150
Your role is to make
that determination.

00:05:27.150 --> 00:05:30.910
A maiden cannot shirk her duty
to make this choice.

00:05:32.760 --> 00:05:35.280
Now, let us begin.

00:05:49.810 --> 00:05:53.060
Stop! Stop it!

00:06:04.940 --> 00:06:09.450
What we just showed you is a portion
of the past that was unknown to you.

00:06:09.990 --> 00:06:14.950
Mankind kills in order to protect
and competes in order to survive.

00:06:15.810 --> 00:06:19.330
For the moment, this arrangement is holding
together in a precarious balance.

00:06:20.240 --> 00:06:25.240
But if this continues unchanged, the day
will come when all life will be extinguished.

00:06:26.340 --> 00:06:29.470
An empty darkness
will fill the skies.

00:06:30.720 --> 00:06:32.220
Is that

00:06:32.630 --> 00:06:35.160
a future that's set in stone?

00:06:35.670 --> 00:06:38.490
Nothing in this world
is set in stone.

00:06:38.600 --> 00:06:40.950
There are only probabilities.

00:06:41.450 --> 00:06:44.980
We exist to make one probability
more likely.

00:06:45.860 --> 00:06:48.610
Allow us to show you
one such example.

00:06:49.630 --> 00:06:53.870
This is a future that
likely awaits your mercenaries.

00:07:18.300 --> 00:07:19.840
Guys?

00:07:21.200 --> 00:07:22.270
Yukimaru!

00:07:59.840 --> 00:08:06.600
This is your first option. Change nothing,
and let the sands of time fall as they may.

00:08:19.650 --> 00:08:20.650
Fena.

00:08:24.110 --> 00:08:25.960
Yukimaru...

00:08:26.830 --> 00:08:28.210
Where are we?

00:08:29.030 --> 00:08:32.090
A world that broke free
of the cycle of death.

00:08:32.670 --> 00:08:34.800
Leaving only hope behind,

00:08:34.830 --> 00:08:39.360
it is an Ark of Time that drifts aimlessly
until the day of rebirth arrives.

00:08:41.990 --> 00:08:44.490
When everything
will be reset.

00:08:45.220 --> 00:08:49.460
It will choose pure souls at random
in order for life to go on

00:08:49.560 --> 00:08:52.200
and consign everything else
to oblivion.

00:08:53.160 --> 00:08:55.050
What do you mean?

00:08:55.150 --> 00:08:57.930
To create anew,
the old will be destroyed.

00:08:58.030 --> 00:09:01.100
Only the wind, the land,
and the sea will remain.

00:09:01.200 --> 00:09:02.660
And...

00:09:06.570 --> 00:09:08.960
Yukimaru?

00:09:10.520 --> 00:09:11.880
I...

00:09:16.140 --> 00:09:19.470
I would never go of your hand again.
That was my vow to you.

00:09:20.550 --> 00:09:25.480
When maidens are reborn, the person she
cherishes most will be at her side.

00:09:27.060 --> 00:09:30.940
The one person deemed to be
most fitting to be her mate.

00:09:31.270 --> 00:09:33.240
But what will happen
to the others?!

00:09:40.870 --> 00:09:42.830
One last thing.

00:09:42.960 --> 00:09:47.360
Once you have chosen, you will have
completed your role as maiden.

00:09:48.660 --> 00:09:52.880
Maidens who have completed their role
lose all their memories.

00:09:54.410 --> 00:09:55.880
Why?

00:09:56.000 --> 00:09:58.490
The human heart is fragile.

00:09:58.580 --> 00:10:01.930
Destruction and further observation
both break the maiden's heart,

00:10:02.030 --> 00:10:03.580
regardless of which
she chooses.

00:10:04.340 --> 00:10:07.270
To Eden, that would
be undesirable.

00:10:08.270 --> 00:10:11.770
For you to create the next
generation of maiden,

00:10:13.050 --> 00:10:16.830
...we require you to continue
your bloodline.

00:10:33.330 --> 00:10:35.250
Why me?

00:10:36.060 --> 00:10:38.050
This is cruel.

00:10:38.640 --> 00:10:40.180
It is because

00:10:40.750 --> 00:10:42.800
making this choice
is what you were born to do.

00:10:45.080 --> 00:10:48.520
I can't do it...
I can't make that choice.

00:10:49.390 --> 00:10:51.460
How could I possibly
make that choice?

00:11:05.100 --> 00:11:07.040
This very moment

00:11:07.550 --> 00:11:10.160
is the reason your heart
began to beat.

00:11:14.130 --> 00:11:17.340
You've made decision after decision
on this voyage, right?

00:11:17.830 --> 00:11:19.590
You can do this, Fena!

00:11:20.640 --> 00:11:22.130
Karin...

00:11:22.520 --> 00:11:23.800
You've gained

00:11:24.660 --> 00:11:27.600
all the experience you need.

00:11:28.110 --> 00:11:31.350
- All that's left now is to choose.
- Yeah!

00:11:31.660 --> 00:11:35.000
- Have some faith in yourself!
- You're our captain, ain't ya?

00:11:35.100 --> 00:11:37.110
- You've got this!
- You've got this!

00:11:37.940 --> 00:11:39.750
- Fena.
- Fena!

00:11:39.860 --> 00:11:41.640
- Fena.
- Fena.

00:11:42.110 --> 00:11:44.140
- Fena.
- Fena!

00:11:44.170 --> 00:11:45.490
Fena.

00:11:45.770 --> 00:11:47.030
Lady Fena!

00:11:47.140 --> 00:11:48.490
Lady Fena!

00:11:50.070 --> 00:11:54.250
I... I'll...

00:12:16.370 --> 00:12:17.680
What the--?

00:12:18.160 --> 00:12:19.250
What's that?

00:12:20.380 --> 00:12:21.750
Come back here!

00:12:24.620 --> 00:12:25.870
This is bad!
It's coming down!

00:12:25.970 --> 00:12:28.690
Crap!
Tsubaki! What do we do?

00:12:29.220 --> 00:12:30.100
We retreat!

00:12:30.420 --> 00:12:31.750
What about Fena and Yukimaru?

00:12:31.810 --> 00:12:33.370
Shouldn't we go help them?!

00:12:33.470 --> 00:12:36.750
If we tried to reach them now,
we'd all die! Besides!

00:12:36.850 --> 00:12:40.360
No matter how bad things have looked,
he's always made it back to us alive!

00:12:40.810 --> 00:12:43.440
Fena has Yukimaru with her!

00:12:45.920 --> 00:12:49.450
Let's trust in Yukimaru.
He'll find a way through this.

00:12:50.190 --> 00:12:51.720
And on that note,

00:12:51.920 --> 00:12:56.070
let's do what we came to do ASAP
and then pick up Yukimaru and Fena.

00:12:56.170 --> 00:12:58.770
If we died here,
it would be a sick joke.

00:13:07.550 --> 00:13:08.590
Fena!

00:13:20.470 --> 00:13:22.280
Fena? Is that you?

00:13:29.050 --> 00:13:30.870
Yukimaru...

00:13:31.850 --> 00:13:33.240
What happened to you?

00:13:33.750 --> 00:13:36.870
Thank goodness...
I'm glad you're okay!

00:13:38.860 --> 00:13:41.250
Let's get out of here!
This place is falling apart!

00:13:41.870 --> 00:13:42.880
Hurry!

00:13:47.650 --> 00:13:50.260
I can't go with you.

00:13:50.920 --> 00:13:53.640
What are... What are you saying?

00:13:55.590 --> 00:13:58.940
I've... I've been running away
from all sorts of memories.

00:13:59.560 --> 00:14:01.840
Things I've tried
not to remember.

00:14:02.700 --> 00:14:06.450
But there was one thing
that I could never forget.

00:14:07.530 --> 00:14:11.010
And that's you.

00:14:12.440 --> 00:14:15.060
I always remembered you.

00:14:15.560 --> 00:14:18.480
My memories of you
were always there with me.

00:14:19.000 --> 00:14:22.020
Of when I sang, when I danced,
when we fished...

00:14:22.120 --> 00:14:23.920
Of when you got mad
because I got carried away.

00:14:24.690 --> 00:14:28.390
I always had faith that you
would come and find me.

00:14:28.670 --> 00:14:31.680
That's what kept me going
even when I was all alone.

00:14:32.250 --> 00:14:37.010
It's because you promised me.
So I was able to keep going.

00:14:38.640 --> 00:14:42.340
And sure enough,
you really did find me!

00:14:42.440 --> 00:14:46.040
You'd gotten taller, and your face
was hidden by that helmet,

00:14:46.140 --> 00:14:47.690
but I knew it was you
the instant I saw you!

00:14:48.440 --> 00:14:50.880
Then I left the island
and met the rest of the guys.

00:14:50.980 --> 00:14:53.190
They're rowdy and love to
goof around together.

00:14:53.770 --> 00:14:58.200
But they're precious friends that I can
always count on when the chips are down.

00:14:58.730 --> 00:15:02.790
Every moment of this journey
is a precious memory to me!

00:15:03.260 --> 00:15:07.210
But all those memories,
all those feelings,

00:15:07.540 --> 00:15:10.210
I'm going to lose them all.

00:15:16.410 --> 00:15:19.000
Listen, Yukimaru.

00:15:22.260 --> 00:15:25.050
Thank you for keeping me
safe all this time.

00:15:25.150 --> 00:15:27.810
I'm sorry I made
so much trouble for you!

00:15:27.890 --> 00:15:29.730
But you don't need to worry
about me anymore!

00:15:30.110 --> 00:15:33.130
I'll try to create a future
where you all survive!

00:15:33.230 --> 00:15:35.970
It might be a really hard future,

00:15:36.050 --> 00:15:38.740
but if anyone can make their way
through it, it's you guys!

00:15:39.060 --> 00:15:41.680
I know it! I know 'cause you
guys are all strong!

00:15:41.780 --> 00:15:44.790
Way, way stronger
than I am!

00:15:45.450 --> 00:15:49.750
Even when I'm gone,
you guys will be... You'll be...

00:15:59.960 --> 00:16:04.770
It's all right. You don't
have to say anything.

00:16:05.520 --> 00:16:10.150
I'll keep you safe.
Come what may,

00:16:10.730 --> 00:16:13.000
...I'll be at your side.

00:16:20.690 --> 00:16:23.390
What am I gonna do, Yukimaru?

00:16:23.490 --> 00:16:28.030
I... I can't believe I'm
gonna stop being me!

00:16:28.280 --> 00:16:31.830
I'm gonna forget about you guys.
I'm gonna forget you, Yukimaru.

00:16:32.140 --> 00:16:34.670
I'm scared... I'm so scared...

00:16:35.730 --> 00:16:41.410
But I can't choose just you...
I like all of you guys so much...

00:16:41.510 --> 00:16:43.680
So I can't do it...

00:16:43.780 --> 00:16:48.010
I tried so hard to think of another way,
but this is the only option.

00:16:48.310 --> 00:16:50.670
But... I'm scared.

00:16:50.810 --> 00:16:52.890
I'll always be with you.

00:16:53.340 --> 00:16:56.200
No matter what happens,
you will always be you.

00:17:01.580 --> 00:17:05.860
I always knew you were nice
deep down, Yukimaru.

00:17:11.540 --> 00:17:12.670
Thank you.

00:17:25.390 --> 00:17:26.730
Fena...

00:17:27.580 --> 00:17:30.860
Thank you for everything,
Yukimaru!

00:17:43.120 --> 00:17:45.080
Don't, Fena!
Don't go!

00:17:45.530 --> 00:17:47.730
Our journey isn't over yet!

00:17:49.410 --> 00:17:54.880
<i>I'm glad that I met you.
That I met all of you.</i>

00:17:56.900 --> 00:18:00.500
I'll never forget you,
not ever!

00:18:01.130 --> 00:18:05.600
No matter where you might be!
Even if you've forgotten who you are!

00:18:06.100 --> 00:18:08.870
I'll find you, no matter what!

00:18:08.970 --> 00:18:12.770
I'll find you,
and I'll make you remember!

00:18:17.900 --> 00:18:20.280
Yukimaru, listen to me.

00:18:22.030 --> 00:18:25.680
I care for you, Yukimaru.

00:18:25.780 --> 00:18:28.540
I have for a long, long time now.

00:18:29.790 --> 00:18:34.040
And I always will.

00:18:34.790 --> 00:18:37.040
Don't go, Fena...

00:18:38.080 --> 00:18:40.090
Don't go.

00:18:41.730 --> 00:18:46.630
FENA!

00:19:12.910 --> 00:19:16.840
Fena! Where are you?!
Fena! Fe--

00:19:39.100 --> 00:19:40.110
Fena...

00:19:53.120 --> 00:19:56.120
Who... are you?

00:19:58.000 --> 00:20:00.200
And who am--

00:20:06.890 --> 00:20:09.890
I'm Yukimaru.

00:20:11.060 --> 00:20:14.140
And you're... Fena.

00:20:16.150 --> 00:20:19.550
Hey! Yukimaru! Fena!

00:20:19.650 --> 00:20:21.290
Fena!

00:20:26.530 --> 00:20:29.890
- Look at this!
- We're glad you made it!

00:20:32.790 --> 00:20:33.720
Fena.

00:20:36.220 --> 00:20:37.760
Let's go back.

00:20:39.000 --> 00:20:41.170
Back to the others.

00:20:49.180 --> 00:20:51.930
- You don't remember anything?
- That's what she says.

00:21:07.700 --> 00:21:09.200
Now, relax your shoulder!

00:21:21.210 --> 00:21:22.590
So, where should we go?

00:21:25.090 --> 00:21:28.370
- Where are you, my beloved?
- What do you even see in that guy?

00:21:28.470 --> 00:21:30.590
You two are such little children!

00:21:31.210 --> 00:21:33.320
- Anything ring any bells, Fena?
- Er...

00:21:33.420 --> 00:21:35.100
Relax, there's no rush!

00:21:57.530 --> 00:22:00.150
Lady Fena!

00:22:02.250 --> 00:22:03.350
- Fena!
- Lady Fena!

00:22:05.250 --> 00:22:07.160
- Fena!
- Lady Fena!

00:22:07.260 --> 00:22:09.810
You look as well as ever!

00:22:12.460 --> 00:22:14.890
Mister! Are you two okay?

00:22:19.390 --> 00:22:20.900
Fena! Keep up!

00:22:21.000 --> 00:22:22.410
Coming!

00:22:32.660 --> 00:22:35.660
Are you hoping to find
scraps of your memories?

00:22:38.830 --> 00:22:40.160
Fena!

00:22:40.510 --> 00:22:43.400
Get a move on, or we really are
gonna leave your butt behind!

00:22:43.500 --> 00:22:45.170
Coming!

00:22:47.170 --> 00:22:49.580
You have to stop
spacing out like that!

00:22:56.180 --> 00:22:57.290
Fena...

00:23:01.720 --> 00:23:03.560
What's this?

00:23:04.090 --> 00:23:07.880
Keep it. Karin forged it
and I honed it.

00:23:07.980 --> 00:23:09.580
I...

00:23:09.640 --> 00:23:11.640
Do you remember it?

00:23:12.950 --> 00:23:15.570
You don't have to try
to force the memories.

00:23:16.110 --> 00:23:19.580
Let them come back to you
bit by bit.

00:23:20.080 --> 00:23:22.670
Whatever happens, I'll protect you.

00:23:24.810 --> 00:23:27.340
I'll always be at your side.

00:23:28.200 --> 00:23:30.090
Yukimaru...

00:23:31.340 --> 00:23:36.170
No matter how much time passes,
even if I grow old and frail,

00:23:36.420 --> 00:23:38.100
my feelings will never change.

00:23:41.620 --> 00:23:43.350
I love you.

00:23:44.220 --> 00:23:46.110
Ow! Fena?

00:24:02.190 --> 00:24:06.570
<i>I've been wanting to hear him
say those words for ages.</i>
